# Canonical input for requirements/locks/release-<platform>-x86_64.txt.
# Regenerate with pip-tools==7.6.1 on the target platform (see requirements/README.md):
# python -m piptools compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements/locks/release-linux-x86_64.txt --strip-extras requirements/release.in
# python -m piptools compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements/locks/release-macos-x86_64.txt --strip-extras requirements/release.in
# python -m piptools compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements/locks/release-windows-x86_64.txt --strip-extras requirements/release.in
#
# The frozen release environment: python-build for wheel/sdist builds,
# pyinstaller for the portable runtime, cyclonedx-bom for SBOM generation,
# setuptools pinned to the pyproject.toml build-system requirement, and the
# runtime dependencies that build_portable.py installs into the frozen env
# from this same lock, plus an explicitly hash-verified pip.
